  "knownDiscrepancies": [
    "The old inspect-button.liquid and the JS-side BUTTON_TOKENS map (styleguide-component-page.js) are two separate, differently-shaped, hand-maintained token listings for the same component (confirmed 2026-08-25) — this spec file replaces both as the single source.",
    "FIXED 2026-08-25: --pos-font-buttons (font-family) was listed as a button token in the old inspect-button.liquid but was not actually applied in pos-button.css. Added font-family: var(--pos-font-buttons) to .pos-button (matches sibling button-family components pos-segmented-control/pos-tile-btn/pos-switch-card, which already had it). Now correctly reflected in shared.typography below.",
    "Primary button's :active state has no dedicated color token (only transform: scale(98%)) — it visually inherits whatever background/border/text the element already had (normal, or hover if the pointer is also hovering). secondary-filled's :active DOES have a dedicated --pos-color-button-secondary-active-background. Possibly intentional, possibly a gap — not changed, just documented.",
    "Primary disabled keeps its box-shadow: var(--pos-primitive-shadow-bevel) (inherited, not reset) while error/success disabled explicitly set box-shadow: none. Possibly intentional, possibly an inconsistency — not changed, just documented.",
    "CORRECTED 2026-08-25: an earlier draft of this spec modeled statusModifier (error/success) and inverted as independently combinable dimensions (3x2 cartesian product per base). Verified against the live doc-site JS (BUTTON_INTENT_CLASSES handler) and pos-button.css that this is wrong — error/success/inverted are mutually exclusive alternatives within a single 'intent' dimension (4 values including none), matching exactly the old inspect-button.liquid's 12 flat variant keys (3 base x 4 intent). No CSS rule exists for an error+inverted or success+inverted combination."
  ],
